Resilience is the correct spelling.

But resilence is interesting as a coined Pantheon term.

* Resilience: The capacity to withstand adversity, adapt, recover, and continue functioning.
* Resilence: We could define it as resilience through silence—the ability to absorb disturbance, preserve one’s internal structure, and recover without immediately reacting.

And there’s a third distinction worth making:

Resilience returns you to functioning.

Antifragility means certain stresses actually improve the system.

ZPC attempts to convert setbacks into reusable knowledge, creating the conditions for that improvement.

So perhaps the progression is:

\text{Endure}\rightarrow\text{Recover}\rightarrow\text{Learn}\rightarrow\text{Evolve}

Was resilence an intentional invention, or were you checking the spelling? Because the invented version has an interesting connection to our Silent Guitar.